--   The ordinary finite RAM handler implements the three-way mathematical oracle for any bit program whose reachable requests have the stated form.
-- statement:
--   The ordinary finite RAM handler implements the three-way mathematical
--   oracle for any bit program whose reachable requests have the stated form.
--   Its persistent arena survives every ordinary instruction and both physical
--   packet transfers. Repeated invocations have an additive address bound.
--
--   This lemma is part of OpenAI's machine-checked proof that rational linear programs can be solved by a strongly polynomial algorithm on a real-number RAM (Smale's ninth problem). It is used in the proof of `OAI.Optimization.LinearProgramming.Compression.NumericROM.solver_of_prefix`.
